libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer a8cb24e (CI release v1.3.276-1-a8cb24e): X11 swapchains keep the
    window size from Present ConfigureNotify events instead of a GetGeometry
    round trip on every surface query. zink's kopper queries the surface
    capabilities every frame, so X11 GL apps no longer wait for the X server
    once per frame (light glmark2 scenes up to ~1.9x faster). Window resizes are
    now reported as VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR from acquire/present, as Mesa's X11 WSI
    does.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:37:17 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * WSI layer 06f7d4d, built with -DWSI_DMABUF_HEAP_COHERENT=ON: dma-buf export
    emulation now works with the cached system heap, which fixes zink without
    kopper (Steam's webhelper sets LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE; its GPU process
    crashed and fell back to SwiftShader).

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:02:19 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Provide cix-gpu-umd (= 2.0.0): packages built for the CIX stack depend on it
    (xwayland +cixmali3), and replacing cix-gpu-umd removed them.

 -- Ivan Podogov <ginkage.uk@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:51:25 +0000

libmali-cix (0.54.1+cix1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Package libmali r54p1 (cix_proprietary 2026Q3 RC2.3) with libEGL_mali,
    a libgbm.so.1 wrapper, the Vulkan WSI layer (CIX defaults), the CSF
    firmware, manifests, a dma-heap udev rule and mali-switch.

